{
  "_comment": [
    "DEV-ONLY: gxwid as a peinit service, run straight from the 9p share.",
    "",
    "gxwid has to be SYSTEM to build gxwi-server's restricted token: a token's",
    "default descriptor grants its own user neither TOKEN_DUPLICATE nor",
    "TOKEN_ASSIGN_PRIMARY, and installing a primary token takes",
    "SeAssignPrimaryTokenPrivilege. The console session drive.py gives us is an",
    "administrator, so the service manager starts gxwid instead.",
    "",
    "dev/run-gxwid.sh is what runs: it picks the compositor and sends output to",
    "the share. No trigger and no restart policy: dev/devloop.sh decides when."
  ],
  "keys": [
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\gxwid",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath", "type": "sz", "data": "/bin/sh" },
        { "name": "Arguments", "type": "multi", "data": ["/share/run-gxwid.sh"] },
        { "name": "Environment", "type": "multi", "data": ["GXWI_LISTEN=0.0.0.0:7780", "GXWI_COMPOSITOR=/tmp/gxwi-compositor"] },
        { "name": "Identity", "type": "sz", "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Readiness", "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName", "type": "sz", "data": "GXWI display server (dev)" },
        { "name": "Description", "type": "sz", "data": "gxwid run from the development share" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
